{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>The sixth day.</b> Scripture added the hei in הַשִּׁשִּׁי at the completion of the work of Creation, to say that He stipulated with them — on condition that Israel accept upon themselves the Five Books of the Torah. Another interpretation: <b>the sixth day</b> — all [of Creation] hung and stood [in suspense] until the sixth day, that is, the sixth of Sivan, which was prepared for the giving of the Torah."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:10.679734304Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}